Linux check in Docker (native arm64 on Apple silicon). Needs a running Docker.
Run: scripts/linux-check/run.sh [SOURCE_DIR] [build test clippy node snap]   (default: this checkout, all steps).
It mounts the source read-only and copies it in; cargo's cache and target live in docker volumes uzu-linux-cargo and uzu-linux-target.
Logs and snaps go to /tmp/linux-check/<folder name>/. Compare clippy by running it on main's checkout too.
Remove the volumes with: docker volume rm uzu-linux-cargo uzu-linux-target
